145: - The recommendation engine uses a **TensorFlow.js model** trained server-side (Python) and exported as a TFJS graph model served from `public/models/crop-scoring/`. The model runs client-side in the browser. A deterministic TypeScript weighted-scoring fallback is used when TFJS fails to load, with `revenue_confidence='low'` and a disclosure banner.
146: - Training data for the TFJS model is generated automatically by running the scoring engine over a dense grid of input tuples; no manual labelling is required. The training script is `specs/003-crop-recommendation/train-model.py`.
147: - Revenue estimates are projections, not guarantees — UI copy must make this explicit per the "UI honesty" constitution principle.
148: - Voice input/output for the recommendation flow is out of scope; text chat and form input only.
